<title>UK: Iraq pumped 1.70 mln bpd in April - OPECNA.</title>
<headline>Iraq pumped 1.70 mln bpd in April - OPECNA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC member Iraq told the group's secretariat that it pumped 1.7 million barrels per day in April, the OPEC news agency OPECNA said on Monday.</p>
<p>Iraq's OPEC quota -- defined by supply to the market rather than wellhead output -- is 1.2 million bpd.</p>
<p>Iraq is allowed to sell oil under a $2 billion United Nations oil-for-food deal.</p>
<p>OPEC defines supply as domestic consumption plus net export sales of crude and products plus withdrawls of stocks held outside national boundaries. Iraq's supply in April was also 1.7 million bpd, OPECNA said.</p>
<p>A Reuters survey of analysts and industry sources found that Iraq produced 1.32 million bpd in April</p>
<p>OPECNA also gave April production figures for the following countries listed below, in million bpd.</p>
<p>COUNTRY	 PRODUCTION   SUPPLY</p>
<p>---------------------------------</p>
<p>ALGERIA	  0.7990	0.7910</p>
<p>INDONESIA	1.3278	 N.A.</p>
<p>IRAQ	     1.7000	1.7000</p>
<p>KUWAIT	   2.0068	2.0078</p>
<p>LIBYA	    1.3940	1.3950</p>
<p>NIGERIA	  1.8314	1.8649</p>
<p>QATAR	    0.4132	0.3952</p>
<p>SAUDI ARABIA   8.0011	8.0017</p>
<p>VENEZUELA	2.4050	 N.A.</p>
<p>N.A. - Not Available</p>
